d average).","Above the world average: 0%–4% of the works per year have an FWCI above 1, most in 2021 (4%).","Not cited: on average 75% of these works have FWCI 0, meaning no citations within their four-year window. That is why many boxes start at 0.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 4 of 4 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2019: mean 0.19, median 0, top work 1.3. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Still counting: works from 2023–2025 have not completed their four-year citation window, so their values will rise. Do not compare them with older years yet.","Small base: the values for 2011–2012, 2016–2018, 2020 and 2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2004, 2013–2014 and 2026 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a box. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."],"citations":["Typical work: works published 2015–2023 have a median of 0–1 citations each; the highest median (1) is in 2015 and 2019.","Most cited works: the top 10% of works published in 2019 have at least 6 citations each, the highest P90 in the chart.","Not yet cited: more than half of the works published 2020–2025 have no citations so far. This is expected for recent works and is not a sign of low quality.","Mean versus median: the mean is above the median in 5 of 5 years, because a few highly cited works pull the average up. The widest gap is 2021: mean 1.5, median 0, top work 39. The median is the better guide to a typical work.","Recent years: works from 2024–2025 have had less than three years to be cited, so their values will rise.","Small base: the values for 2011–2012, 2016–2018, 2020 and 2025 are based on only 10–29 works (lighter box or hollow point), so read them with care.","Few works: 2004, 2013–2014 and 2026 have fewer than 10 works, too few for a band. Each of those works is drawn as a dot."]}}}